Comment: DRAFT of milestone M1 (live view); completed at M7 with every library the
 later milestones open (FFmpeg libav*, alsa-lib, libpulse). The application is linked
 against the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the CardputerZero launcher by M5Stack
 (Copyright M5Stack Technology CO LTD, MIT) and LVGL (Copyright LVGL Kft, MIT), which
 are part of the binary and are therefore listed in its Copyright field below. The
 fonts it draws with are the launcher's, read at run time from
 /usr/share/APPLaunch/share/font; none is shipped in this package.
 .
 The V4L2 capture code, the fake camera, the conversions, the measurements and the
 pages are the app's own code, written from scratch for this project from the Linux
 V4L2 API documentation (the kernel header videodev2.h is used at build time only) and
 the TurboJPEG API documentation. The settings file helpers (JSON, atomic writes) are
 copied from the Vinyl and Cassette apps of this repository (MIT, the same author).
 .
 System libraries the binary is linked against at build time (named NEEDED in the
 binary): libfreetype6 (FreeType License or GPL-2.0-or-later), libinput10 (MIT),
 libxkbcommon0 (MIT), libstdc++6 and libgcc-s1 (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime
 Library Exception 3.1). They are not copied into this package.
 .
 Library opened at run time with dlopen, from the system; neither linked into the
 binary nor shipped in this package (the package depends on it):
  - libturbojpeg.so.0, the TurboJPEG API of libjpeg-turbo (Copyright the libjpeg-turbo
    Project and others; IJG License, BSD-3-Clause and zlib License), used to decode the
    camera's MJPEG frames (and, for the fake camera only, to encode its test card).
    Package libturbojpeg0.
 Program run at run time when present: vcgencmd (Raspberry Pi firmware tools), for its
 get_throttled flags when the kernel has no get_throttled node.

